        "node_id": "n_1_8398c9",
        "thought_text": "Model the problem as placing K blue balls into N positions such that they form exactly i contiguous groups, which requires choosing i groups of blue balls and distributing the remaining N-K red balls into the i+1 possible gaps (before, between, and after groups) using stars and bars, then multiplying by the ways to arrange the internal blue balls (which is 1 since they are indistinguishable) and summing over valid configurations.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794588810.6199048
      },
